# Run artefacts — regenerated by every sweep, and large.
# .jaato-eval-workspaces held 4.6 GB of per-arm git worktrees; an arm that ran
# `git add -A` from the wrong cwd once committed the bare repo-cache mirror
# into the harness's own history, which is why this entry comes first.
.jaato-eval-workspaces/
results*.jsonl
sweep_run*.log
*_trace*.log
client_trace.log

# Session state — per-run, and it carries model output and file backups.
.jaato/logs/
.jaato/sessions/
**/.jaato/logs/
**/.jaato/sessions/

# Credentials — NEVER commit.  The openrouter key lives in ~/.jaato/, resolved
# daemon-side from a pass:// URI; nothing here should ever hold a literal.
*_auth.json
.env
!.env.example

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated caches, not source.  The template index embeds `generated_at` and
# an absolute `source_path`, so a committed copy points at whichever machine
# last ran a sweep — ours pointed at the directory this repo was extracted
# FROM.  Both are rebuilt on demand by the template plugin.
.jaato/templates/
**/.jaato/templates/
.jaato/waypoints.json
**/.jaato/waypoints.json

# The consolidated document the Pages site renders.  Generated from sweeps/ by
# tools/site/collect.py on every publish, and it embeds `generated_at` — a
# committed copy is a snapshot claiming to be the live one, same reason the
# template caches above are not source.
site/data.json
